## Common commands

```bash
# Search the project wiki
/wiki-search "<query>"

# Add an external reference (article, doc, video) to the wiki
/wiki-update <url>

# Wrap up the current session
/wrap-up

# Promote what's staged
/wiki-promote --review
```

## Where memory lives

| Layer | Where |
|---|---|
| **Session** (this conversation) | Claude Code context window |
| **Short-term** (recent sessions) | agentmemory (background MCP server) |
| **Long-term** (durable knowledge) | {{WIKI_PATH}}/ |
| **Raw** (immutable log) | {{LLM_WIKI_PATH}}/raw/ |

## Don't

- Don't paste session transcripts into wiki entries — `/wrap-up` distills them. Transcripts go to `{{LLM_WIKI_PATH}}/raw/sessions/`.
- Don't promote directly to `{{WIKI_PATH}}/` — always stage in `{{WIKI_PATH}}/_inbox/proposed/` and let `/wiki-promote` move them.
- Don't edit `_MAP.md` or `_INDEX.md` by hand — they're auto-generated.
